===== Page 21 of 41 =====
Computing Jacobian geometrically

• Instead of computing Jacobian analytically,
   we can take a geometric approach to
   compute it

• Let’s say we are just concerned with the end
   effector position p for now.
     – This also implies that the Jacobian will be an 3×N
         matrix where N is the number of DOFs
     – For each DOF of a joint, we analyze how p would
         change if the DOF changes

 ILE5030 Computer Animation and Special Effects 25S   21

