===== Page 26 of 41 =====
Jacobian may not be invertible!
• Non-square matrix
     – pseudo inverse
• Singularity
     – causes infinite joint velocities
     – occurs when any        cannot achieve               that is not
         perpendicular to the arm




 ILE5030 Computer Animation and Special Effects 25S   26

===== Page 27 of 41 =====
Remedy to Singularity Problem

• Add redundancy
   – add more joints to the original joint chain
   (more DOFs are added)
   – Jacobian matrix is not square


• Use pseudo inverse of Jacobian!




 ILE5030 Computer Animation and Special Effects 25S   27

===== Page 28 of 41 =====
Pseudo Inverse of the Jacobian




 ILE5030 Computer Animation and Special Effects 25S   28

===== Page 29 of 41 =====
Adding more control to IK
• Pseudo inverse computes one of many
  possible solutions that minimize joint angle
  velocities
• IK using pseudo inverse Jacobian may not
  provide natural poses
• A control term can be added to the pseudo
  inverse Jacobian solution
• The control term should not add anything to the
  velocities, that is
                                                           control term

 ILE5030 Computer Animation and Special Effects 25S   29

